  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a majestic image of Mount Everest with text that reflects on the tragic deaths of climbers, suggesting that these individuals were once highly motivated. The concluding line, 'stay lazy, my friends,' is intended to be ironic and provocative, encouraging viewers to avoid the risks associated with extreme ambition. While not explicitly targeting any specific group with hate or abuse, the meme's message can be interpreted as harmful because it trivializes the immense physical and mental effort, as well as the risks, involved in attempting to climb Everest. It may discourage people from pursuing challenging goals by implying that such endeavors are ultimately futile or that the risks outweigh the rewards, potentially undermining motivation and resilience. The meme's intent is to provoke thought through irony, but its message can be seen as dismissive of human perseverance and achievement, which may have a negative psychological impact on those who value ambition and challenge.",
